<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:22:21Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Republicans put Trump center stage in US midterms gamble</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:887020023fd2070fc681ebf54c2f67a217c569c76b756e769dee50bbe4963873</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:21:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T19:04:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/republicans-put-trump-center-stage-in-us-midterms-gamble--87590ae3ef88.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/republicans-put-trump-center-stage-in-us-midterms-gamble" /><summary type="html">US Republicans open an extraordinary midterm convention in Dallas on Wednesday betting that putting Donald Trump at the center of their campaign can rescue a party facing grim election forecasts -- despite the president's deeply negative approval ratings. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Whose space is it? Europe scrambles as US rules satellite race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f263ee4a8fae7ff47d295f3f1c0bdcd119b1619935d615b26302fadabd642f18</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:21:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T18:35:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260909-whose-space-is-it-europe-scrambles-as-us-rules-satellite-race--507bb145af5a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260909-whose-space-is-it-europe-scrambles-as-us-rules-satellite-race" /><summary type="html">With the digital age comes the scramble for minerals below us and the scramble to master the heavens above us. Donald Trump wants a thousand rocket launches a year and with SpaceX’s reusable modules leading the way, the United States towers over the competition. It’s why for instance Ukraine’s president has to beg Elon Musk to use his Starlink low orbit satellite system to take out the Russian cruise missile launchers.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Iran strikes ships, expands no-go zone outside Hormuz strait</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c4cebc4ad8d183a65066e060ea4055dae12147c4c0cf73273c0ddb22c11191c</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:21:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T18:30:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iran-strikes-ships-expands-no-go-zone-outside-hormuz-strait--ad14b4ac2e24.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/iran-strikes-ships-expands-no-go-zone-outside-hormuz-strait" /><summary type="html">Iran said it attacked more than a dozen vessels trying to pass through the Strait of Hormuz on Wednesday, as it announced an expansion of a no-go zone outside the strategic waterway it has blockaded for months. The fresh attacks and fighting with the United States have sent oil prices above $100 per barrel again as Tehran chokes off the strait and Washington presses a counter-blockade of Iranian ports. FRANCE 24's Reza Sayah reports from Tehran.</summary></entry><entry><title>How a French Foreign Legion soldier dramatically escaped Colombian captors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:69967210eba254bf9590299e31600a5447f5f90c42f87b034bb5404bb6bb2d22</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:21:30Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T16:17:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-how-a-french-foreign-legion-soldier-dramatically-escaped-colombian-captors--eda72903bbbd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-how-a-french-foreign-legion-soldier-dramatically-escaped-colombian-captors" /><summary type="html">A French Foreign Legion soldier kidnapped by Colombian guerrillas escaped after nearly a month in captivity by overpowering a guard, jumping into a river with his hands tied and trekking for four days through the Andes to reach safety, according to a Colombian military source.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Kenya's crackdown on foreign workers raises concern among Burundians</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d9b711db006ba4f2b0f1b9356b85183a6fe0de249ac5cf6391ae5009edb194c1</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:21:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T15:47:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-kenya-s-crackdown-on-foreign-workers-raises-concern-among-burundians--45769dfceaec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-kenya-s-crackdown-on-foreign-workers-raises-concern-among-burundians" /><summary type="html">Some 16,000 Burundian refugees and asylum seekers live in Kenya, and many of them make a living through informal jobs – as carpenters, motorcycle taxi drivers, or clothing vendors. But since Monday, many have been afraid to go to work, and are now looking to leave the country. The reason: remarks made by Kenya’s president, which have sparked deep concern within the Burundian community. More from our correspondent Bastien Renouil.</summary></entry><entry><title>Céline Dion's return to France: A French love affair</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:96001c3056c48f93abc5c6d14721dbef57bfe19488b2bdbf33586d42bde90ac2</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:21:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T15:33:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-c_line-dion-s-return-to-france-a-french-love-affair--9bf6220bbfc0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-c%C3%A9line-dion-s-return-to-france-a-french-love-affair" /><summary type="html">Céline Dion’s hotly anticipated return to the stage is scheduled for this Saturday in Paris – the first of more than 16 concerts in the French capital in September and October. The shows mark a major milestone for 58-year-old Dion after years away from touring due to a rare neurological disorder. FRANCE 24's Aurore Cloé Dupuis tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Macron summit seeks boost for European space despite no-shows</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1c18b469e15239ccf4e7395e055190ac10e95bcddcc87e18dc4e1bb4605850a3</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:21:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T15:32:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-macron-summit-seeks-boost-for-european-space-despite-no-shows--7b96a3288314.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-macron-summit-seeks-boost-for-european-space-despite-no-shows" /><summary type="html">France is pressing ahead with a space summit shunned by the US tech giants and hampered by a lower-than-expected turnout from European leaders as President Emmanuel Macron seeks a stronger role for Europe in the competitive maelstrom of space. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Angela Diffley tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>NY failed to disclose what it knew on 'toxic air' after 9/11</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b3bd1a927b02730704c01982dda20023323a9ff1a0153277b775b4d72fbb689b</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:21:42Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T15:30:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-ny-failed-to-disclose-what-it-knew-on-toxic-air-after-9-11--c93d28c12ee6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-ny-failed-to-disclose-what-it-knew-on-toxic-air-after-9-11" /><summary type="html">New York Mayor Zohran Mamdani announced on Tuesday the release of tens of thousands of documents showing the city did not disclose all it knew about air toxicity after 9/11. The release comes ahead of the 25th anniversary of the September 11, 2001, attacks that killed 2,977 people in the United States, mostly in the collapse of the Twin Towers in New York. In the years since, more than 9,400 have died from illnesses linked to their exposure to the area, according to a federal medical monitoring program.</summary></entry><entry><title>Peru: 38 skeletons unearthed in ancient tomb</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:35943d0a308f3639c268b86dcf3a931814b403aab2cadf1e77b436f679dd6f7e</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:21:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T15:21:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-peru-38-skeletons-unearthed-in-ancient-tomb--4f2dbe101ee4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-peru-38-skeletons-unearthed-in-ancient-tomb" /><summary type="html">Archaeologists in Peru have discovered a near-intact pre-Incan tomb, containing the skeletons of 38 individuals, along with gold and copper objects. The remains include those of an elite member of the Chimu civilization, which flourished between 900 and 1470 AD.</summary></entry><entry><title>France's far-right National Rally fires policeman from security team over racist, sexist comments</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c83c55edf0f0e791e8616fe8c784804107f5529ec4c1f63fe8c3c3a9341afc8b</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:21:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T15:16:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20260909-france-s-far-right-national-rally-fires-policeman-from-security-team-over-racist-sexist-com--bd390f39c0d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260909-france-s-far-right-national-rally-fires-policeman-from-security-team-over-racist-sexist-comments" /><summary type="html">France's far-right National Rally (RN) has expelled a policeman from its ranks after bodycam footage of him making racist, homophobic and sexist remarks was published on Wednesday. The controversy threatens to revive scrutiny of the party's efforts to distance itself from its extremist past ahead of next year's presidential election.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>‘Call My Agent’ returns: George Clooney, Eva Longoria guest star in French film spinoff</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1afc65838f195050ff59704d971766fcfa0bbb526bec785e398fe5df0459049b</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:21:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T14:29:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260909-call-my-agent-returns-george-clooney-eva-longoria-guest-star-in-french-film-spinoff--a01ae944c586.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260909-call-my-agent-returns-george-clooney-eva-longoria-guest-star-in-french-film-spinoff" /><summary type="html">Manon Kerjean, FRANCE 24's film critic highlights some of her picks among the French films in competition at the 83rd Venice International Film Festival. She also looks at new releases in French cinema: "15/18", a film set in a psychiatric unit which tackles mental health and "A Woman's Life" – a film starring Cesar-winning actress Léa Drucker as a woman whose organized life is upended by the arrival of a stranger. She also previews "The Unknown", a film by Arthur Hariri about two strangers who wake up in each other's bodies. Finally, she gives her thoughts on a highly anticipated film, "Call my Agent", which picks up five years after the end of the hit TV series on Netflix.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>Pope merchandise flies off shelves as France gears up for pontiff's visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8ab440780fe5533ec5000a8557cdf00079f14b76dbdf6712b626ccf0a5820a31</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:21:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T14:03:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-pope-merchandise-flies-off-shelves-as-france-gears-up-for-pontiff-s-visit--24ed093720ae.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-pope-merchandise-flies-off-shelves-as-france-gears-up-for-pontiff-s-visit" /><summary type="html">Tshirts, mugs and rosaries... These are just a few of the items available in the range of merchandise hitting souvenir shops ahead of Pope Leo XIV’s much anticipated visit to the northeastern French city of Metz on 28th September. The items have proved hugely popular, with some flying off the shelves quicker than shopkeepers can stock them.</summary></entry><entry><title>Modern warfare: Ukraine racing to develop new interceptor drones</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b71d7723529070d1d7e9415298b249c9e9fd3a20b99cbfbd87861031d9a16da</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:21:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T14:00:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-modern-warfare-ukraine-racing-to-develop-new-interceptor-drones--e4ff102be357.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-modern-warfare-ukraine-racing-to-develop-new-interceptor-drones" /><summary type="html">In recent weeks, Russia has been deploying jet-powered Shahed-type drones against Ukraine, presenting a new challenge for Ukrainian air defences. Kyiv is now working to develop interceptor drones capable of matching their speed and bringing them down. FRANCE 24’s Gulliver Cragg is in Kielce, Poland, at one of Europe’s largest arms fairs. He is joined by Roman Hapachylo, CEO of DoD Solution, one of the companies developing these technologies.</summary></entry><entry><title>12 countries including France, UK and Canada to sanction Israeli settlements</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:39db0062912afd6167d48571284c556b63309725029c7ab5246729212eea04ce</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:22:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T13:59:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-12-countries-including-france-uk-and-canada-to-sanction-israeli-settlements--d74ec0936279.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-12-countries-including-france-uk-and-canada-to-sanction-israeli-settlements" /><summary type="html">Twelve countries including Britain, Canada and France announced Tuesday they would sanction trade with Israeli settlements in the West Bank, after increasing attacks by settlers against Palestinians in the occupied territory. Denmark, Finland, Iceland, Ireland, Norway, Poland, Portugal, Spain, and Sweden also plan to issue restrictions on trade with the settlements, the nations' foreign ministers said in a joint statement. The action follows weeks of increasing attacks by Israeli settlers against Palestinian villages in the illegally occupied territory that has drawn widespread condemnation from the international community.</summary></entry><entry><title>Putin and Trump discuss Ukraine in 'extremely frank' call</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a142d52f25fcd0ed8aadc3bfd4aa1d6915ae97eb1face763fa17a06c16db0d6c</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:22:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T13:55:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-putin-and-trump-discuss-ukraine-in-extremely-frank-call--82aa21c6d7ad.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-putin-and-trump-discuss-ukraine-in-extremely-frank-call" /><summary type="html">Russian President Vladimir Putin and US counterpart Donald Trump on Tuesday discussed the Ukraine conflict in an "extremely frank" and constructive hour-long phone call, the Kremlin said. It came after US negotiators Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner visited Moscow and Kyiv over the weekend in an attempt to kickstart long-stalled US efforts to end the fighting. Washington has been pushing for fresh face-to-face talks between Moscow and Kyiv.</summary></entry><entry><title>'We need to put the tech bros back in their box,' says Baroness Beeban Kidron</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae87226cdca95a054b42481c8ac0f977b6a296dbf978a6a56c5659d54afffe6e</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:22:06Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T13:54:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/we-need-to-put-the-tech-bros-back-in-their-box-says-baroness-beeban-kidron--652490c9cf2c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/we-need-to-put-the-tech-bros-back-in-their-box-says-baroness-beeban-kidron" /><summary type="html">In this edition, one of the world’s leading campaigners against the increasing influence of Big Tech describes it as “generational injustice against children”. Baroness Beeban Kidron abandoned her thirty-year career as a world-renowned filmmaker, to challenge Big Tech, though she says it’s not necessarily the technology that is at fault, but the way we use it. In conversation with FRANCE 24’s Stuart Norval, she talks about her book “Users – How big tech took control and How to Fight back”.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>Suspected migrant smugglers go on trial in Paris over mass drowning in Channel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a8d0204e35ee23a378a0b16c3da2640eba943dd8a93f469dbf44886d7f970d9d</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:22:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T13:53:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-suspected-migrant-smugglers-go-on-trial-in-paris-over-mass-drowning-in-channel--2d434207b13c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-suspected-migrant-smugglers-go-on-trial-in-paris-over-mass-drowning-in-channel" /><summary type="html">Fourteen people went on trial in France on Tuesday over the death of at least 31 people in the Channel in 2021, the deadliest accident involving asylum seekers trying to reach the English coast. The trial carries particular significance because of the high death toll and the sheer number of civil parties involved, 114 in all, including victims' families. Some of them travelled from Erbil in Iraq's Kurdistan region to testify.</summary></entry><entry><title>French Riviera heist: Renoir paintings stolen from French museum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ecc477eee4c5d462887f7dd48f38cb09e352b5a1a64b32b96dcc4960b6a092b3</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:22:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T13:51:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-french-riviera-heist-renoir-paintings-stolen-from-french-museum--63e977309dd9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-french-riviera-heist-renoir-paintings-stolen-from-french-museum" /><summary type="html">Police were on Tuesday hunting for two thieves who escaped with two Renoir paintings from a museum in southern France, after abandoning two others in its garden as they fled, a mayor said. The heist is the latest in a string of such robberies in France including the daylight theft last year of crown jewellery valued at around $100 million from the Louvre in Paris.</summary></entry><entry><title>France’s record heatwave pushes champagne alcohol levels to historic high</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5b2163e05a59b4ff7d5b425e4005b7842483bce7c7434abaa5e5f7bbfba021d9</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:22:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T13:49:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20260909-france-s-record-heatwave-pushes-champagne-alcohol-levels-to-historic-high--6681c215a131.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260909-france-s-record-heatwave-pushes-champagne-alcohol-levels-to-historic-high" /><summary type="html">France’s record-breaking summer heat has forced champagne producers to contend with unusually high sugar levels in grapes, forcing authorities to allow alcohol content of up to 15 percent in the region’s sparkling wine for the first time. Champagne is usually capped at 13 percent.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>The Times: 'Counterproductive' sanctions on Israel don't match the 'theatrical rhetoric'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9d7e9992d3eda543deaac7b4e758cb3cf4a2075fcec52049d760ce911ab26216</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:22:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T13:35:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260909-the-times-counterproductive-sanctions-on-israel-don-t-match-the-theatrical-rhetoric--24a57d7cc6c6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260909-the-times-counterproductive-sanctions-on-israel-don-t-match-the-theatrical-rhetoric" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Wednesday, September 9: British papers are reacting to the sanctions imposed on Israel. Next: Israeli papers discuss Haaretz's October 7 revelatory investigation. Also: CDs are back! Finally, South Park renames itself to South America to mock Trump.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Rungis market chief on supply chains and feeding the world</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7dd5131f4bb702d75fc795b3edc57cec50ee6c6e078c9a11a5953b853952fc7c</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:22:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T13:05:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20260909-rungis-market-chief-on-supply-chains-and-feeding-the-world--b449a157d7e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20260909-rungis-market-chief-on-supply-chains-and-feeding-the-world" /><summary type="html">In today’s edition, FRANCE 24’s Delano D'Souza speaks with the man at the heart of France's food supply chain. Stéphane Layani is the head of the Rungis wholesale food market – the largest of its kind in Europe – and chairman of the World Union of Wholesale Markets. Earlier this year Layani came out with a book titled Le Monde a faim, or "The World is Hungry" in English. In his interview, he gives his perspective on how France's food system will transform in the coming years.</summary><category term="Entre Nous" /></entry><entry><title>The world's third global aerospace market: India's civil aviation sector takes off</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:db97a017fde5430f9cf389b5a518ee3ade49fd4c550bd5da6836ce994e1687f6</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T12:34:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260909-the-world-s-third-global-aerospace-market-india-s-civil-aviation-sector-takes-off--663d5050bc0d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260909-the-world-s-third-global-aerospace-market-india-s-civil-aviation-sector-takes-off" /><summary type="html">The aviation sector is one of the India's strongest-performing industries. More than 70 airports have been built over the past decade, and the country counts over 400 million air passengers annually. In just ten years, India has become the world's third-largest aviation market, behind China and the United States.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia's Vucic calls snap elections after nearly two years of protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ac8dfab86b03889d62a7ccb2eb12ee0906758d3102852acb3d88faf37bf1e22f</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T12:15:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260909-serbia-vucic-calls-snap-elections-after-nearly-two-years-protests--5f70b882a781.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260909-serbia-vucic-calls-snap-elections-after-nearly-two-years-protests" /><summary type="html">Serbian President Aleksandar Vucic on Wednesday called snap parliamentary elections for October 25. They are expected to be a key test of his right-wing populist Serbian Progressive Party after nearly two years of student-led anti-corruption protests.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Iran attacks US base after American strikes on tankers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cdc4aacb35688138843e184bfe252be5f55b924be3c47ad141e4f93b557fb804</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T11:43:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-iran-attacks-us-base-after-american-strikes-on-tankers--4a8c873638da.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-iran-attacks-us-base-after-american-strikes-on-tankers" /><summary type="html">Iran said it fired ballistic missiles at a US base in Jordan early Wednesday, in retaliation for US strikes on Iranian oil tankers in the Gulf of Oman and near Kharg Island, off Iran’s coast. The US said five Iranian tankers were destroyed.</summary></entry></feed>
